From: David J. Vandenburgh <david@vandenburgh.co>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6prm: probe asynchronously

The GPR bus adds the PRM service from glink's rx worker right after the
APM service, while the ADSP channel opens. prm_probe() calls
q6apm_is_adsp_ready(), which sends APM_CMD_GET_SPF_STATE through q6apm
and takes q6apm's lock to do it. When q6apm's own probe has already
started (it probes asynchronously since "ASoC: qcom: q6apm: probe
asynchronously"), it holds that lock while it waits for its own
GET_SPF_STATE response, and that response can only be delivered by the
rx worker prm_probe() is now blocking. Both wait out the full 5 second
timeout:

  qcom-apm gprsvc:service:2:1: CMD timeout for [1001021] opcode

and the sound card registers 5 seconds late. Whether it happens depends
on which probe gets there first: when prm_probe() runs before q6apm has
set g_apm it defers instead, and the retry runs off the rx worker. On a
Retroid Pocket 6 it hit four boots in a row on 7.3.6.

Probe q6prm asynchronously too, so nothing in the rx worker waits on
the DSP.

Signed-off-by: David J. Vandenburgh <david@vandenburgh.co>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6prm.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6prm.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6prm.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6prm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6prm.c
@@ -245,6 +245,14 @@
 	.driver = {
 		.name = "qcom-prm",
 		.of_match_table = of_match_ptr(prm_device_id),
+		/*
+		 * Like q6apm, the PRM service is added from glink's rx worker.
+		 * Its probe asks q6apm for the DSP state, which waits on q6apm's
+		 * lock while q6apm's own probe holds it for the same answer, and
+		 * that answer can only arrive through the rx worker this probe
+		 * would be blocking.
+		 */
+		.probe_type = PROBE_PREFER_ASYNCHRONOUS,
 	},
 };
 
